From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:11:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: glymur-hp-omnibook-ultra-kg0xxx: no lid
 wake while open

On every exit from CX power collapse in s2idle the lid line sees an
edge, so with the lid open the system wakes again a few seconds into
every suspend. Keep the lid wakeup unarmed for a suspend entered with
the lid open; with the lid closed, opening it still wakes the system.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-hp-omnibook-ultra-kg0xxx.dts | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-hp-omnibook-ultra-kg0xxx.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-hp-omnibook-ultra-kg0xxx.dts
index 7af48732f7f0..0b9621387765 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-hp-omnibook-ultra-kg0xxx.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-hp-omnibook-ultra-kg0xxx.dts
@@ -63,6 +63,7 @@ switch-lid {
 			linux,code = <SW_LID>;
 			wakeup-source;
 			wakeup-event-action = <EV_ACT_DEASSERTED>;
+			wakeup-on-state-change;
 		};
 	};
 
